Creating a complete Vitis HLS implementation of an MNIST handwritten digit recognition neural network is quite complex and beyond the scope of this platform due to its length and complexity. However, I can provide you with a simplified example that demonstrates how to implement a basic neural network using Vitis HLS.

For simplicity, let's consider a very small neural network with one hidden layer for demonstration purposes. This example will not achieve high accuracy but serves as a starting point for understanding how to use Vitis HLS for implementing neural networks.

First, ensure you have installed Xilinx Vitis HLS and set up your development environment.

Here's a simple example of a neural network with one input layer (784 neurons), one hidden layer (128 neurons), and one output layer (10 neurons). The activation function used here is ReLU (Rectified Linear Unit).

```cpp
#include <ap_fixed.h>
#include <hls_stream.h>

// Define data types
typedef ap_fixed<16, 8> fixed_t;

// Neural Network Parameters
const int INPUT_SIZE = 784;
const int HIDDEN_SIZE = 128;
const int OUTPUT_SIZE = 10;

// Weight matrices and bias vectors
fixed_t weights_input_hidden[INPUT_SIZE][HIDDEN_SIZE];
fixed_t biases_hidden[HIDDEN_SIZE];
fixed_t weights_hidden_output[HIDDEN_SIZE][OUTPUT_SIZE];
fixed_t biases_output[OUTPUT_SIZE];

// Input and Output streams
hls::stream<fixed_t> in_data;
hls::stream<fixed_t> out_data;

void relu(fixed_t &x) {
    if (x < 0)
        x = 0;
}

void forward_propagation() {
#pragma HLS INTERFACE axis port=in_data
#pragma HLS INTERFACE axis port=out_data

    // Hidden Layer
    fixed_t hidden_layer[HIDDEN_SIZE] = {0};
    for (int i = 0; i < HIDDEN_SIZE; ++i) {
#pragma HLS UNROLL
        for (int j = 0; j < INPUT_SIZE; ++j) {
            hidden_layer[i] += in_data.read() * weights_input_hidden[j][i];
        }
        hidden_layer[i] += biases_hidden[i];
        relu(hidden_layer[i]);
    }

    // Output Layer
    fixed_t output_layer[OUTPUT_SIZE] = {0};
    for (int i = 0; i < OUTPUT_SIZE; ++i) {
#pragma HLS UNROLL
        for (int j = 0; j < HIDDEN_SIZE; ++j) {
            output_layer[i] += hidden_layer[j] * weights_hidden_output[j][i];
        }
        output_layer[i] += biases_output[i];
    }

    // Write output to stream
    for (int i = 0; i < OUTPUT_SIZE; ++i) {
#pragma HLS PIPELINE II=1
        out_data.write(output_layer[i]);
    }
}
```

